al strategies (such as behavioral modifications, sensory stimulation, or structured routines) have failed, and the patient''''s behaviors are severe, distressing, and/or pose an immediate threat of harm to themselves or others. If used, they must be started at the lowest possible dose, monitored closely for side effects (e.g., extrapyramidal symptoms, QT prolongation), and tapered for discontinuation at the earliest opportunity.'),
